''Radii of Circumscribed, Inscribed and Escribed Circles of a Triangle.'' Let <math>R</math> denote the radius of the circumscribed circle, <math>r</math> of the inscribed, and <math>r_1</math>, <math>r_2</math>, <math>r_3</math> of the escribed circles of a triangle <math>ABC</math>; the values of these radii are given by the following formulae:—
{{block center|<math>R=abc/4S=a/2\sin A</math>,}}
{{block center|<math>r=S/s=(s-a)\tan\tfrac{1}{2}A=4R\sin\tfrac{1}{2}A\ \sin\tfrac{1}{2}B\ \sin\tfrac{1}{2}C</math>,}}
